  <CaseSection id="process" title="Build process">
    <CaseProse>
      <p>
        The wake word is detected on the device, so no audio leaves the device to
        listen for “Logatot.” Providers asked about this first.
      </p>
      <p>
        Speech is matched against known phrases and the class roster without AI. A
        live model would be slower and could log a nap that never happened. The
        rules either match an entry or send it to review.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI runs only when a child is added. It lists likely mishearings of the name,
        and corrections in the review queue add to that list. Spanish is translated
        before matching, so one phrase set covers both languages.
      </p>
    </CaseProse>

    <CaseCards label="Services" items={integrations.map((s) => ({ icon: s.icon, title: s.name, body: s.role }))} />

    <CaseProse class="mt-12">
      <p>
        Attendance is calculated from check-in history, so it always matches what
        happened. A wrong headcount is a licensing problem.
      </p>
    </CaseProse>

    <div class="mt-12">
      <Heading level={3} visual="h2" class="mb-6">System-level decisions</Heading>
      <ul class="grid gap-x-8 gap-y-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {structural.map((item) => (
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-ink">
            <Icon name={item.icon} size={20} class="shrink-0 text-ink-muted" />
            {item.label}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <Fragment slot="media">
      <Container width="wide" class="mt-16">
        {flowSet('11-flow-voice-logging').map((flow) => (
          <Plate title={flow.title} caption={flow.note} src={sheet(flow.slug)} alt={flow.alt} />
        ))}
      </Container>
    </Fragment>
  </CaseSection>

